# Agent dependency hygiene (spec 060)

Simultaneous agents share one checkout. Cleanup of dependency trees is a **human** action.

## Forbidden unless the user explicitly asks this turn

- **npm:** local `npm ci`, `rm -rf node_modules`, `npm cache clean`, prune/wipe “to fix,” deleting lockfiles to regenerate
- **Go:** `go clean -cache`, `go clean -modcache`, wiping module/build caches as repair
- **Python:** deleting `.venv`/`venv`, `pip cache purge`, bulk `__pycache__` / `.pytest_cache` wipes as repair
- Any “delete install tree and reinstall from scratch” recovery loop

On install/build failure: report the error; fix **source**. Do not auto-clean.

## Allowed

- **Frontend pre-push (spec 005):** reuse `frontend/node_modules` when present; `npm install` only if missing or `package.json` / `package-lock.json` changed this turn; then `npm run build`. Never local `npm ci` (CI-only).
- **Go:** `go test` / `go build`; `go mod download`/`tidy` only when needed.
- **Python:** reuse existing venv; `pip install` only when env missing or requirements/lock changed.

## Soft concurrency

No flock. Do not escalate races with cleanup. Full contract: `specs/060-agent-dep-hygiene/spec.md`.
